---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

const SUPPORT = "support@lector.dev";
---

<Base
  title="Refund Policy | Lector"
  description="A 14-day money-back guarantee on cloud plans, cancel any time, and a full refund if you switch to the free self-hosted version mid-cycle."
>
  <header class="docs-header">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">lector</a> / refunds</p>
      <h1>Refund Policy</h1>
      <p class="post-meta">Last updated 8 July 2026</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="docs-body">
      <p>
        This policy covers the managed cloud plans. The self-hosted version of
        Lector is free and open source — there's nothing to pay and nothing to
        refund.
      </p>

      <div class="callout">
        <p>
          <strong>Short version.</strong> 14-day money-back guarantee on your
          first payment, cancel any time, and if you decide to switch to the free
          self-hosted version part-way through a cycle, we'll refund the rest of
          it. No hard feelings.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>14-day money-back guarantee</h2>
      <p>
        If you're not happy with a cloud plan, email us within
        <strong>14 days</strong> of your first payment and we'll refund it in
        full — no questions asked.
      </p>

      <h2>Cancel any time</h2>
      <p>
        You can cancel whenever you like. Cancellation stops any future billing,
        and you keep access until the end of the period you've already paid for.
        Outside the situations below, we don't normally refund the unused part of
        a current billing period.
      </p>

      <h2>Switching to self-hosting</h2>
      <p>
        Lector is self-hostable and free, and we'd never want the subscription to
        trap you. <strong>If you cancel mid-cycle to move to the self-hosted
        version, email us and we'll refund the unused remainder of your current
        period.</strong> We'll happily point you at the{" "}
        <a href="/docs/installation/">setup docs</a> too.
      </p>

      <h2>Annual plans</h2>
      <p>
        Cancelled an annual plan early? On request, we'll refund the unused whole
        months remaining in your term.
      </p>

      <h2>How refunds are processed</h2>
      <p>
        Payments and refunds are handled by{" "}
        <a href="https://www.paddle.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Paddle</a>,
        our merchant of record. Approved refunds are returned to your original
        payment method through Paddle, and typically take a few business days to
        appear. This policy doesn't affect any statutory rights you have, such as
        consumer guarantees under the Australian Consumer Law or the EU right of
        withdrawal.
      </p>

      <h2>Requesting a refund</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT}`}>{SUPPORT}</a> from the address on your
        account, or use the customer portal link on your Paddle receipt. You can
        also use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Lector is operated by
        Luke Boyle.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
